BEGIN_PGML
Answer these questions about the practical difficulties that might arise when plotting points and setting the scales on the two axes.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
What would be the difficulty with trying to plot [`(12,4)\text{,}`] [`(13,5)\text{,}`] and [`(310,208)`] all on the same graph?

[@ANS(essay_cmp()); essay_box(6,76)@]* [@essay_help()@]*

END_PGML

##########
# Solution
##########

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Answers will vary, but the issue is that once you set the scale on both axes so that both [`(12,4)`] and [`(310,208)`] will appear, then [`(13,5)`] will appear to be so close to [`(12,4)`] that it will be challenging to draw them both and make it clear they are two different points.

END_PGML_SOLUTION

